																		In the very distant future, &quot;What is Sunday?&quot;  AD...
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ihp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1267048); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1267048&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605795250" alt="Ihp" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1267048)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ihp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1267048); return false;" >Ihp</a></span> <span class="odate time_1530417628 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">01 Jul 2018 04:00</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3856833">
									

<p>So this is still a little unfinished&#8212; I had issues uploading a pair of the pictographs (Issue on my end, internet and computer has been screwy because of air conditioners running at full blast) and may be forced to host them on a site like Imgur in the next couple of days. I'll try to localize most of them before the 4th.</p>
<p>Work on this started literally eight or so minutes after the 4000 contest was announced. I thought &quot;Hey, the SETI Arecibo message is pretty cool. Might be neat to base an SCP around a future civilization discovering the Foundation's equivalent of it.&quot;</p>
<p>And let me tell you, in the course of writing and researching this, I've found out something: SETI. Are. Idiots. The Arecibo image is based on the flawed assumption that Aliens are going to know what binary is&#8212; for all we know, a civilization it reaches may have invented radio to pick it up, but may not have developed binary. Maybe they've made a more efficient system that's rendered binary obsolete.</p>
<p>That aside, coming up with pictograms to depict most of this stuff was fun, and challenging. Probably the hardest to covey was the one from 173&#8212; there's no universal sign for &quot;kill&quot;. Some worms can survive with their heads cut off, for instance. So, I chose potassium cyanide as a substance that's almost universally toxic to carbon-based life to convey &quot;oh shit, this thing kills people&quot;.<br />
<span style="font-size:0%;">I see you reading between the lines. Look at <a href="/scp-1050">SCP-1050</a>. One of my favorite SCPs, for what the destroyer is.</span><br />
Credit where credit is due: <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/toa-vine" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2023146); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2023146&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1530419561" alt="Toa_Vine" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2023146)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/toa-vine" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2023146); return false;">Toa_Vine</a></span>, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sir-baubius" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2200357); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2200357&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1530419561" alt="Sir Baubius" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2200357)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sir-baubius" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2200357); return false;">Sir Baubius</a></span>, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dog-teeth" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3116447); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3116447&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1530419561" alt="Dog Teeth" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3116447)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dog-teeth" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3116447); return false;">Dog Teeth</a></span>, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rimple" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2320004); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2320004&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1530419561" alt="Rimple" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2320004)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rimple" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2320004); return false;">Rimple</a></span>, and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anaxagoras" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1019930); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1019930&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1530419561" alt="Anaxagoras" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1019930)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anaxagoras" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1019930); return false;">Anaxagoras</a></span> all critted this, and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/scpcrnp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3927912); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3927912&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1530419561" alt="scpcrnp" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3927912)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/scpcrnp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3927912); return false;">scpcrnp</a></span> graciously let me use their code from <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-sqrt-1-j">SCP-sqrt-1-J</a> for this article. Several more may have critted; If I have forgotten you, feel free to say so.</p>
<p><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arecibo_message.svg">Arecibo message</a> image taken from Wikimedia commons. All other images of my own creation.</p>
<p>E: Also I just realized that this is my 101st article. Woo!</p>

